* Thermo-optic ring bank: four WDM rings locked to their channels against thermal crosstalk
* and self-heating.
*
* Four rings of models/multiphysics/ringbank/ring_parts.va on a 0.8 nm channel grid (lasers at
* 1550.0, 1550.8, 1551.6, 1552.4 nm, 1 mW each), each fabricated 0.25-0.30 nm blue of its
* channel. Each sits on a 4000 K/W, 1 ms thermal node, neighbours coupled through 16000 K/W
* (a quarter of a ring's own conductance: the thermal crosstalk). A heater under each ring is
* driven by a PI lock holding that ring's drop power at 40 % of its input (`lock frac=0.4`), on
* the blue side of the resonance, the side a heater reaches from cold. The loops close at 1 ms.
*
* Two disturbances:
*   30 ms  channel 1's laser hops +0.2 nm. Ring 1 must warm by ~2.914 K to follow, its heater
*          rises, and the heat leaking to ring 2 is cancelled by ring 2's heater backing off.
*   60 ms  channel 3's laser steps from 1 to 4 mW. The lock holds the drop at 40 % of the new
*          input; at the same detuning the ring absorbs 3 x 0.044 mW more, which its heater
*          gives back.
* Closed form: with every ring held at its lock temperature, the thermal network is linear and
* the heater powers follow from it (docs/examples/multiphysics/ring_plots.py computes them):
*   at 30 ms  heater 1 +0.9105 mW = (1/4000 + 1/16000) W/K x 2.914 K; heater 2 -0.1821 mW
*             = -2.914 K / 16000 K/W; heaters 3 and 4 unchanged (ring 2's lock stops the heat).
*   at 60 ms  heater 3 -0.1320 mW = -eta (Q_e/Q_i) 0.4 x 3 mW; nothing else moves.
* Measured at 2.16.1+1: all four lock (rings 1/4 at 4.92 ms, 2/3 at 6.37 ms); after the hop
* heater 1 +0.9106 mW, heater 2 -0.1821 mW; after the power step heater 3 -0.1320 mW; every drop
* back at 40 % of its input.
* This deck is what found 2.16.1's fix: the dense solver called this well-posed 72-unknown system
* singular at the 30 ms hop, because its residual test did not allow for rows written in 1/s
* (~1e11) beside rows in W/K (~1e-4).
* Plot: python docs/examples/multiphysics/ring_plots.py target/release/va-cli
* Run: va-cli sim circuits/multiphysics/ring_bank.net --model models/multiphysics/ringbank --tran --report in1,in2,in3,in4,dr1,dr2,dr3,dr4,u1,u2,u3,u4
VW1 w1 gnd PWL(0 1550.0 30m 1550.0 30.01m 1550.2)
VW2 w2 gnd DC 1550.8
VW3 w3 gnd DC 1551.6
VW4 w4 gnd DC 1552.4
VP1 p1 gnd DC 1
VP2 p2 gnd DC 1
VP3 p3 gnd PWL(0 1 60m 1 60.01m 4)
VP4 p4 gnd DC 1
XL1 p1 w1 in1 wl1 laser
XL2 p2 w2 in2 wl2 laser
XL3 p3 w3 in3 wl3 laser
XL4 p4 w4 in4 wl4 laser
XR1 in1 wl1 th1 dr1 t1 ring lambda0=1549.75
XR2 in2 wl2 th2 dr2 t2 ring lambda0=1550.50
XR3 in3 wl3 th3 dr3 t3 ring lambda0=1551.30
XR4 in4 wl4 th4 dr4 t4 ring lambda0=1552.15
XC1 t1 thermal_cap
XC2 t2 thermal_cap
XC3 t3 thermal_cap
XC4 t4 thermal_cap
XG1 t1 gnd thermal_res
XG2 t2 gnd thermal_res
XG3 t3 gnd thermal_res
XG4 t4 gnd thermal_res
XX12 t1 t2 thermal_res r=16000
XX23 t2 t3 thermal_res r=16000
XX34 t3 t4 thermal_res r=16000
XH1 u1 t1 heater
XH2 u2 t2 heater
XH3 u3 t3 heater
XH4 u4 t4 heater
XK1 in1 dr1 u1 lock kp=5 ki=3e3
XK2 in2 dr2 u2 lock kp=5 ki=3e3
XK3 in3 dr3 u3 lock kp=5 ki=3e3
XK4 in4 dr4 u4 lock kp=5 ki=3e3
.tran 50u 100m
.end
